# SRG-APP-000233-WSR-000146  -  CAT II
# The web server document directory must be in a separate partition from the
# web servers system files.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000233-WSR-000146
group:           V-206408
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
cci:             CCI-001084
control_rev5:    SC-3

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise locates all index data under a single configurable root,
                 SPLUNK_DB, and each index's bucket paths are expressed relative to that
                 root, so index data can be placed outside the installation tree and on its
                 own file system. Whether the resulting path is a distinct partition is a
                 file system fact the application cannot read.

governs:         indexes.conf - The indexes data is stored in, how large they may grow and how long data
                 is kept.
governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_DB non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index_name>] coldPath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-indexers-and-indexer-clusters/10.4/manage-index-storage/use-multiple-partitions-for-index-data
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index_name>] homePath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-indexers-and-indexer-clusters/10.4/manage-index-storage/use-multiple-partitions-for-index-data
vendor:          indexes.conf [<index_name>] thawedPath https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-indexers-and-indexer-clusters/10.4/manage-index-storage/configure-index-storage
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_DB https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether the path SPLUNK_DB resolves to is a separate partition or mount
                 point - operating system file system layout and mount table
external:        Partition sizing and the mount options applied to the index file system -
                 operating system
external:        The location of the installation tree itself relative to the operating
                 system's own file systems - operating system
external:        Whether index data sits on a partition separate from the Splunk system
                 files, which is a filesystem property that no indexes.conf path expresses;
                 the application-layer share is that splunk-launch.conf SPLUNK_DB is set
                 and resolves outside the installation directory.

citation:        splunk-launch.conf.spec:67-73 (SPLUNK_DB = <string>, "The fully qualified
                 path to the directory containing the index directories", primarily used by
                 paths expressed in indexes.conf); indexes.conf.spec:412-418 (homePath,
                 best practice "homePath = $SPLUNK_DB/$_index_name/db");
                 indexes.conf.spec:446-452 (coldPath, best practice
                 "$SPLUNK_DB/$_index_name/colddb"); indexes.conf.spec:468-474 (thawedPath,
                 required, cannot contain a volume reference). tstatsHomePath is excluded
                 because indexes.conf.spec:531-536 requires it to be defined in terms of a
                 volume definition rather than a direct path.
finding:         Index data is not separated from the product's system files to the extent
                 the application allows: SPLUNK_DB is unset or expressed under the
                 installation directory, or an index's home, cold or thawed path is set to
                 a fixed path rather than one relative to the index root.
